235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (While Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\) excel at extracting spatial and spectral features from a spectrogram, the Gated Recurrent Unit \(GRU\) is integrated to model the signal's temporal dynamics. By processing these features as a time-series sequence, the GRU effectively captures the progression of melody and rhythm. Cho et al. \(2014\) have proposed that this architecture leverages gating mechanisms to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem inherent in standard RNNs, enabling the model to represent long-term dependencies and accurately track the evolution of musical emotion throughout the audio duration.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
